A||||6||DiggityDan||Engine noise problem(long but important)||||1||
Z||000000||DiggityDan||05-07-2000||01:14 AM||||My car needs help. I've got an 85 GT v6, 4 speed. It ran pretty good, I've only driven it a short time. <BR>After I bought it, I put a clutch, shifter cable, and shocks an struts in it.After all of this work, i drove it from my dad's shop were I worked on it, to where I live now - about a 2.5 hour drive. The car ran great, got about 20 mpg going 80 with the air conditioner on. <BR>The next after the trip, I took the car out, just playing around a little and I guess I pushed it to hard. The engine has acquired a tick, sounds like its either a lifter tap or maybe an exhaust leak - my front manifold is leaking, different thread. It comes in about 2200 rpm and just gets increasingly faster and louder with speed. My oil pressure has stayed around the same area, except tonight I noticed that when I turned left, the oil gauge would dip down almost to the red, and then when I straightened out, it would level out again.<BR>I know this post is long and rambling, but I am kind of at a loss at this one, I can't really pin point it. All of your help would be appreciated. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||05-07-2000||01:32 AM||||is your oil level at the correct amount?<P>I know the lifters and rockers will make noise when there isn't any oil getting up there.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DiggityDan||05-07-2000||01:38 AM||||Oil level is perfect............pulled all the spark plugs, and they were all in great shape. No oil or gas on the plugs, they are burning just about perfect.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phaeton||05-07-2000||02:56 AM||||Oil pickup tubes are often just press fit into place, reasoning being that since they are always sucking they should only work tighter, not looser.<P>If it did somehow work loose then air could be sucked in when the top of the tube got uncovered during cornering, that happens even with full oil.<P>It wouldn't fall completely out right away as the pickup end would hit the pan before the top cleared.<P>This has happened once in my lifetime to a small block chevy, so what are the odds?||||reg||12
Z||000004||80's BOY||05-07-2000||09:59 AM||||definitely the oil pickup tube. it fell out. mine did the same. call it luck, but on my 3.1 rebuild i considered tack welding it to the pump while the block was out. people told me they never would fall out so i installed it and went about my business. i did some scca racing in january and on the way home, the same problem you have with the oil pressure occurred. after a few hard turns, seems the tube fell out anyway. had a friend with a fiber optic camera (i'm lucky) so we pulled the plug and looked up in the pan. proved my case immediately. now i just add an extra quart of oil so i don't get so nervous on those hard turns. also added some Slick 50 for added protection just in case.||||reg||3
Z||000005||DiggityDan||05-07-2000||04:09 PM||||**** ....that makes perfect sense. I hit a bump a little hard and when I hit the pavement that's when all this ****  started. Definately explains why my oil pressure is so jacked right now. I'm going to get the oil pan off later this week, I will probably just JB Weld that thing in. Thanks Phaeton and 80's boy....great help.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||05-08-2000||06:02 PM||||I had an 88 Pontiac 6000, 2.8 V6. The oil pickup fell off the pump on it twice. The pump sits so low in the pan that the hole remains in oil most of the time. Except on a left turn that is...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The first time it was under warranty and the dealership "fixed" it. They never told me what was really wrong... some story about trash in the pickup! <P>Anyway several years and many thousand miles later it did it again. That's when I had to do it myself and found out what the problem REALLY was. The tube/pump had some really bad looking attempts at welding on it. Not easy to weld a thin steel tube to a cast iron housing I guess... It might have actually lasted the life of the engine anyway except they ground 90% of the part of the weld that was actually doing anything back off trying to clean it up. I know he people working for dealerships run the range from highly qualified professionals to idiots. No doubt in my mind which end of the spectrum I got that time!!!<P>I put on a new pump and pickup, used lock-tite to "help" the pressed fit and had no more problems.<BR>||||reg||1
